User Management

The User Management feature in the Supervisor Dashboard allows supervisors in WADEPS to
assign Create Record permissions and Supervisor permissions for your agency.
To manage access:

    Select Manage Users from the Active Users in Your Agency Tile on the right of the screen.

This will take you to the Agency Profile and User Management page. A list of your agency
personnel and their assigned permissions will appear.

                                                                                                                                                                                                             98
                                                                                                                                                                                          99

    Permission Levels:
         Read Only - User can only view their own use of force reports.
         CAD Upload Only - User can upload CAD data only.
         Create Records - User can create and submit for supervisor approval their own use of force
         reports in WADEPS (via Create a Record).
         Admin - User has full permissions, including:
              Submitting reports on behalf of others
              Uploading CAD data
              Conducting Supervisor Review
              Completing Administrative Follow-up
              Assigning supervisor permissions
              To grant Create Record permissions:

    Assigning Permissions:
         Locate the user in the personnel list.
         Use the drop-down menu in the permissions column.
         Select the appropriate permission level.

Adding New Users

In some cases, the personnel that needs create and approve permissions may not be on the agency
profile and user management page. This could occur for two primary reasons:

    An officer's primary employment is with another agency.
    The individual does not have a WADEPS account.

