CAD DATA IN WADEPS

WADEPS uses Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) data to provide context for use of force (UOF)
events. By linking UOF reports with CAD information, WADEPS can calculate UOF rates based on
call volume and call types.
Agencies without CAD data will not have UOF rates generated. In these cases, WADEPS will report
UOF incidents as counts only.
There are three key steps for uploading CAD data into WADEPS:

    CAD Mapping
    Download the CAD Data Template
    Upload CAD Data into WADEPS

                                                                                                                                                                                                                   109
                                                                                                                                                                                        110

CAD Mapping

WADEPS is working with public safety answering points (PSAPs) and agencies to reduce data-entry
burden by mapping CAD call type labels to WADEPS Initial Incident Type and Initial Incident Detail.
Mapping ensures:

    Call types are classified consistently across agencies.
    Agency-to-agency comparisons are meaningful.
    WADEPS analysis accurately reflects the context of calls for service. WADEPS will complete
    initial mapping of CAD call type codes and then coordinate with PSAPS and agencies to confirm
    accuracy. This collaborative process ensures that each call type is assigned to the correct Initial
    Incident Type and Initial Incident Detail.

   CAD Mapping Resources

    For more information about CAD mapping or to learn how your agency can participate, please
    visit: https://wadeps.org/the-data/cad-data/.

CAD Data Upload

To upload CAD data:
    Select the CAD Upload button at the top center of the screen.

                                                                                                                                                                                                                   110
                                                                                                                                                                                        111

   Important

         If the CAD Upload button does not appear on your screen, you do not currently have
         permission to upload CAD Data.
         Only personnel with supervisor permissions in WADEPS can grant access.
         Contact your agency point of contact (POC) to request the necessary permissions.
    This will take you to the CAD Upload page.

Download the CAD Data Template

    Select the Download Template button on the left side of the screen underneath the "Download
    CAD Data Template."

Entering Data in the CAD Data Template

    Open the template and select the Template worksheet on the bottom of the spreadsheet.

                                                                                                                                                                                                                    111
                                                                                                                                                                                        112

There are 5 columns to complete in the CAD Template:

incident_id

    Enter the Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) incident number associated with the UOF event.

agency_name

    Enter the name of your agency.

record_creation_time

    Enter the record creation time from your CAD system.Use the following format: mm/dd/yyyy
    hh:mm:ss AM/PM.

         Example: 08/15/2025 02:34:55 PM

original_call_type

    Enter the original call type or nature of call code from your CAD system.

city

    Enter the city where the use of force event occurred.

   Important

         Agencies using CAD header or column data formats that differ from our standard may
         experience challenges during the upload process. We understand the importance of
         maintaining your existing systems and workflows. To support this, our team can work with
         you to create a customized mapping solution. This allows you to continue using your native
         CAD headers while still enabling successful data uploads. If your agencyʼs CAD format
         differs from the standard, please contact us to discuss your header structure. We will help
         identify the best approach to ensure a smooth and efficient integration.
         All five fields are required for each record.

CAD Reporting Requirement

CAD Uploads use year-to-date basis to ensure any changes or corrections in agency systems are
accurately reflected in WADEPS.

    Agencies must upload CAD Data within 5 business days at the start of each month.
    Each file must include data from January 1st through the end of the prior month. Once
    processed, any errors will appear on the Notifications page. Click the ! icon in the top right
    corner to review them.

                                                                                                                                                                                                                   112
                                                                                                                                                                                        113

   Example:

         For the October reporting period, provide data from January 1, 2025, through September
         30, 2025.
         For the November reporting period, provide data from January 1, 2025, through October
         31, 2025.

Uploading the CAD Data Template

To upload your CAD Data Template, complete the following steps:
    Save your file as either an Excel (.xlsx) or CSV (.csv) format.
    If you are using Excel and choose to save the file as CSV:
         Ensure that any commas used within data fields are properly enclosed. For example, in the
         officer name field: "James, John H."
         Excel typically does this for you during the save process.
    If you are working directly in a CSV or text editor (e.g. Notepad or similar) to enter or edit data,
    do not use commas within any data fields, as this may disrupt the upload formatting.
    Select the CAD Upload button in the top center of your screen. Drag and drop your saved file in
    Upload Files OR select the choose a file button.
    You will receive a pop-up message that your file has successfully uploaded.
    If there are any, they will be in your Notifications page (! icon at the top right of the screen).

                                                                                                                                                                                                                   113
                                                                                                                                                                                        114

Frequently Asked Questions

How to report a use of force event that is currently under internal
investigation?

    If the use of force event is under internal investigation, it still must be reported to WADEPS using
    the online reporting tool. This can only be reported using the Create a Record feature. The first
    question will ask if the officerʼs use of force (UOF) on the subject is under internal investigation
    and/or referred for independent investigation by the Office of Independent Investigations (OII)
    or the Independent Investigation Team (IIT). Select Internal Investigation and provide limited
    event details as directed. Please note the Batch Upload feature cannot be used for these
    events.

How to report a use of force event that is currently been referred
for independent investigation by the Office of Independent
Investigations (OII) or the Independent Investigation Team (IIT)?

    If the use of force event has been referred for independent investigation, it still must be reported
    to WADEPS using the online reporting tool. This can only be reported using the Create a Record
    feature. The first question will ask if the officerʼs use of force (UOF) on the subject is under
    internal investigation and/or referred for independent investigation by the Office of Independent
    Investigations (OII) or the Independent Investigation Team (IIT). Select Internal Investigation and
    provide limited event details as directed. Please note the Batch Upload feature cannot be used
    for these events. Are PIT maneuvers a reportable use of force?
    Yes, PIT maneuvers are a reportable use of force. Chapter 10.118 RCW includes "used a vehicle
    to intentionally strike a person or other vehicle" as a reportable use of force type regardless of
    injury. WADEPS includes an additional field so agencies can specify if the strike was a PIT
    maneuver under 40 MPH, a PIT maneuver 40 MPH or above, or not a PIT maneuver.

How do we report the use of force event if the subject is unknown?

    If the subject is unknown, the event must still be reported in WADEPS. Unknown will be entered
    into the subject id. Unknown can also be selected for all the subject demographic fields. The age
    field is numeric, enter 999 in this field to indicate an unknown subject.

How do we report the use of force event when a chemical agent (e.g. tear gas)
is deployed against a crowd control measure?

    When a chemical agent (e.g. tear gas) is deployed as a crowd control measure—not at specific
    individuals—follow these steps in WADEPS:

         Enter "crowd" in the Subject ID field.
         Select "Unknown" for all subject-related fields (e.g., age, race and ethnicity, gender, etc.).

                                                                                                                                                                                                                   114
                                                                                                                                                                                        115

    If multiple officers deployed tear gas, a separate use of force report for each officer must be
    submitted to WADEPS.
    If there are known subjects who were directly affected or targeted (e.g. a subject was arrested or
    received medical attention):

         Submit a separate use of force report for each know subject, including all subject-related
         information.

What if the “under investigationˮ status isnʼt known at the time of reporting, or
an investigation starts days or weeks after the UOF event?

    WADEPS allows some flexibility for investigations that begin during or after the initial reporting
    period depending if the investigation occurs within the 30-day reporting period or after.

         Within the 30-Day Reporting Period
              If the investigation status changes while your report is still in progress:
                  Delete the draft record (before supervisor approval).
                  Re-enter the record using Create a Record and select the appropriate investigative
                   entity (Internal Investigation, OII, IIT).
                   This pauses the record and stops compliance timers.
              Complete the UOF report when ready: Once the investigation determination is finalized,
              return to the record and fill in all required fields within 30 days.
              Submit as normal: Route the record through the standard approval workflow.

         After the 30-Day Reporting Period
              If an investigation occurs after the report has been approved:
                  Records are locked: you cannot edit an approved report.
                  Separate Administrative Reporting: Report the administrative outcome (Administrative
                   Follow-Up Items) within 30 days of investigation determination.

    Key Takeaways
         You can pause reporting when you expect an investigation but donʼt yet have full information.
         Pausing is only available before supervisor approval.
         Remember there are two processes:
              Initial UOF Event reporting
              Administrative Follow-Up Items

